Here is the commit message:
OOZIE-2536 Hadoop's cleanup of local directory in uber mode
 causing failures (satishsaley via rohini)

Here is the root cause:
The bug is caused by Hadoop's cleanup process of local directories in uber mode, which fails when the required configuration file (`PROPAGATION_CONF_XML`) does not exist. This absence leads to issues during the execution of jobs, as the cleanup process relies on this configuration file to function correctly.

Here is the patch:
 package org.apache.oozie.action.hadoop;

+import java.io.File;
 import java.io.IOException;


+    public OozieLauncherOutputCommitter() {
+        File propConf = new File(LauncherMapper.PROPAGATION_CONF_XML);
+        if (!propConf.exists()) {
+            try {
+                propConf.createNewFile();
+            }
+            catch (IOException e) {
+                System.out.println("Failed to create " + LauncherMapper.PROPAGATION_CONF_XML);
+                e.printStackTrace(System.err);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     @Override
     public void setupJob(JobContext jobContext) throws IOException {
     }



